reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-1-// reference/src/semantics/iter.k — MPY-ITER
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k:2:// The iterator protocol, DECLARATION ONLY. Each iterable's #iterNext case lives in that
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-3-// iterable's own module (list/tuple/str in their modules, rangeObj in range.k, zip in
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-4-// builtins.k). Consumers (the for-loop, `x in _`, sum/all/any/max/min) import this.
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-5-
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-6-module MPY-ITER
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-7-  imports MPY-CORE
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k:8:  syntax KItem ::= #iterNext(Iterable) | "#iterDone" | #iterYield(Val, Iterable)
reference-semantics/semantics/iter.k-9-endmodule
